{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1554711835,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MzAzMTg0MDI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3300","origin":"github"},"title":"GitRepo.get_content_info() performance issue","message":"In https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/cc3a9e6dd56eaeb0f1c9c14dc1a3bc3d453fe881/datalad/support/gitrepo.py#L2918 we homogenize the report of `symlinks` in a dataset repository to `type='file'` if we can determine that that symlink is an annex pointer.\n\nIt turns out that this has a real performance hit. In a repo with 33k files doing this increases the runtime of a `status()` from 4s to 12s.\n\nHowever, simply disabling this will impact the convenience-level felt in high-level code, as this was done to homogenize cross-platform/mode feel when dealing with annex'ed files.\n\nUsing pathlib would immediately gain 2s speedup (but see comment in code re PY3.5).\n\nSwitch to `os.readlink()` based test seems to be the obvious improvement: runtime ~5s","files":null}]}